   "summary": "John's great-grandfather; born in Tamaqua c.1904, son of Henry J. Meier and Anna Higgins; a coal-company clerk and supervisor in Wilkes-Barre all his documented life; died 4 Jul 1963.",
   "bio": "William F. Meier was born about 1904 in Tamaqua, Schuylkill County, PA (birthplace on his 1926 marriage application; his ages are 6 in Apr 1910, 15 in Jan 1920, 22 in Apr 1926, 26 in 1930, 45 in 1950 and 59 at death in Jul 1963). FamilySearch (LTHM-B3G) dates him 1905–1963; the Ancestry tree says 1904–1963. Henry's family was in Tamaqua in 1905–06 (brother Joseph John born there 30 Jun 1906). In 1910 he was 'William, son, 6' at 14 Mill Street, Wilkes-Barre Ward 14; in 1920 'William, son, 15, errand boy at a drug store' at 298 Barney St, Ward 15. On 16 Apr 1926 he swore marriage-licence application No. 10768 in Luzerne County: William F. Meier, clerk, born Tamaqua, PA, residing at 16 Barney St, Wilkes-Barre, age 22, not previously married; father 'Henry', residing in Wilkes-Barre, moulder, birthplace given as 'Penna.' (an error — Henry was German-born); mother 'Anna', maiden name 'Higgins'. The bride was Florence Louise Pringle, clerk, born Plymouth, of 28 Huston St, age 22, daughter of Addison (carpenter) and Catherine Heffernan. They married 20 Apr 1926, by Rev. D. W. McCarthy, Wilkes-Barre. In 1930 (ED 40-261, sheet 23B, 55 Cedar Street) he was 'Wm F., head, 26', clerk in a 'coal office', with Florence (25), William (about 3) and James (1 9/12); Addison Pringle's family at 28 Huston St is on the same census sheet. In 1950 (ED 40-102, sheet 2, house 55) he was 'William F., head, 45, supervisor at a coal company' (company abbreviation unclear), with Florence (45), William Jr. (23), James C. (21) and Barbara Ann (14). In 1943 'Mrs. William Meier' of Wilkes-Barre was listed among Addison Pringle's survivors (the only anchor found in the first report). He died 4 Jul 1963 in Wilkes-Barre (PA death index 1963: 'MEIER, WILLIAM F; age 59; WLKS BRE; county 40 [Luzerne]; died 07/04/63; file 071200; residence code 40001'). A search snippet also shows a 'William F Meier, b. 26 Dec 1905, d. 8 Jan 1964' and a 'William A. Meier, b. 1904, d. 10 Mar 1964 in Pennsylvania' — probably other men; the 1963 death is kept. His WWII draft card (1940s 'old man's' registration, b. 1904) was not reachable. Possible infant daughter: 'Meier, Florence Irene', funeral from Wilkes-Barre, notice published 11/12 Oct 1933 (not in the 1933 PA death index under M600; speculative).",
