   "summary": "John's 2nd great-grandmother; born 1867 in the Schuylkill County coal town of New Philadelphia to an Irish-born father; wife of Henry J. Meier.",
   "bio": "Annie A. Higgins was born 2 Oct 1867 in New Philadelphia, Schuylkill County, PA (marriage docket No. 11054). She was living in Hazleton when she married Henry J. Meier there on 1 Mar 1892 (licence 10 Feb 1892). In 1910 (14 Mill St, Wilkes-Barre) she was 42, born PA, father born Ireland, mother born PA, mother of 7 children of whom 6 were living. She appears as Anna (52) in 1920 at 298 Barney St and Anna A. (72) in 1940 at 16 Barney St. FamilySearch (LBV1-4CM) calls her 'Anna Agnes', died 6 Oct 1951 in Wilkes-Barre, buried St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Twp. (Find a Grave index QVG4-98JK); it names her parents as William Higgins and Mary Ann Reilly, but the parent profiles have no sources and web searches for them (and for a William Higgins of New Philadelphia) found nothing. The Ancestry tree shows 'Anna Higgins (Deceased)' with parents empty. Higgins was a common Irish Catholic name in the Freeland–Drifton–Hazleton coal patch in the 1890s (e.g. William Higgins of Ridge and Main streets, Freeland; Andrew Higgins of Freeland, a Hazleton clerk; Frank Higgins m. Hannah Thomas at St. Ann's, Freeland; a 'Miss Annie Higgins' who married John Shovlin at Silver Brook in 1891 — none linked).",
