   "bio": "Charity Davenport was a daughter of Capt. Thomas Davenport (1682-1759) of Philipstown; which of his wives was her mother is unchecked (the second wife Elizabeth was 'believed' to be a Leggett). In 1752 her father deeded Goshen-precinct land to 'Charity Lamoree, wife of John Lamoree', next to her brother Oliver Davenport. The 1919 Lamoureux Record calls her 'Charity Danforth' - 'Danforth's' was simply how people in the Hudson Highlands said 'Davenport's'; it even appears on Erskine's Revolutionary map of West Point.",
   "sources": [
    "Giles & Franklin, Thomas Davenport, Philipstown Pioneer 1682-1759, and his Descendants (1962): https://archive.org/details/thomasdavenportp00gile (also HathiTrust wu.89066038563: https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89066038563&view=1up&seq=395) pp. xvii, 355-361",
    "WikiTree Lamoreaux-21 (Thomas Lamoreaux; full will transcription citing FamilySearch images of Luzerne Will Book A): https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lamoreaux-21 ; PAGenWeb will transcription: http://www.pagenweb.org/~luzerne/patk/tomlam.htm",
    "A. J. Lamoureux, André Lamoureux, the Huguenot Emigrant, and Family (The Lamoureux Record no. 1, 1919): https://archive.org/details/andrlamoureuxh00lamouoft"
   ],
